fieldValues.move:
Make the unit of tension affirmation a domain's three lines. In one domain view the owner sees, for each line:
- the inherited axis (the parent's, or the base Act/Observe, Disrupt/Stabilise, Focus/Zoom out) as a working default that needs no tick;
- the local trade-off placed on that line, with its local pole names and yang pole;
- the problems that concern each pole.

The parent and sibling domains are shown beside it, and a 2×2 of two lines with real problems in each corner tests orthogonality.

Placing a trade-off on a line is the one act. It forks the tension with its nested poles and writes the axis-in-domain record. Every other tension stays a suggestion, shown in context: confidence comes from what rests on it, never from a tick.

It is built in stages, each shippable alone:
0. repair the ground (poles nested under their tension, affirmed structure pointing at affirmed poles);
1. the structural rules declared in the method package and checked by the engine;
2. a generic record-in-context card over the engine's context_record;
3. one-act tension affirm (srs-web#581);
4. the domain lines view, piloted on Evidence-backed writing;
5. weight tiers, so only foundational placements reach the owner;
6. movement over time.
